From add2fa047fe107d2b311a17540bab393517ea57d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:36:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(v2): never let a skill through on an unverified
 permission outcome

The v2 permission bridge treated every create failure as 'nothing was shown' and resolved. That let a skill run after its tool call was cancelled, and after the server had parked the request but the response body was lost. It also subscribed to the reply only after the create response arrived, so a fast answer was lost and the call waited forever, and an aborted wait left its event subscription running.

The bridge now picks the request id itself and listens for the reply before it creates the request. An aborted call always rejects and withdraws its request. After a failed create it checks whether the request is parked (HTTP list, then the plugin host): parked means wait for the answer, unverifiable means reject, and only a verified-unparked failure (retried once) takes the documented fail-open, which OMO_V2_PERMISSION_FAIL_CLOSED=1 turns into a rejection. A parked request that disappears without an observed reply rejects instead of hanging. The create has its own deadline, the subscription is always closed, netstat runs through the windows-hide spawn helper instead of a raw Bun.spawn, and the server password is sent only to a listener that refused an anonymous request the way OpenCode does.
